      "source": [
        "# Notebook 02: EDA Enriquecido y Visualización de Outfits\n",
        "\n",
        **Propósito:** Ampliar el análisis exploratorio del dataset Garments2Look con estadísticas de imágenes, distribuciones de resoluciones y una galería visual de outfits. Este notebook continúa donde dejó el 01 y prepara los datos para el preprocesamiento DWPose del siguiente paso.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Objetos cargados desde Notebook 01:** `outfits`, `outfits_mvp`, `garments_per_outfit`, `cat_cnt`, `n`, `prom`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Verificación de objetos cargados desde Notebook 01\n",
        "print(f\"📦 Total de outfits: {len(outfits)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"🎯 Outfits MVP (≤6 prendas): {len(outfits_mvp)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"👕 Promedio de prendas/outfit: {prom:.2f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Repetimos algunos cálculos por si el kernel cambió\n",
        "from collections import Counter\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n# Distribución de prendas por outfit (ya la tínhamos, pero la volvemos a ver)\n",
        "garments_per_outfit = [len(o.get('garments', [])) for o in outfits]\n",
        "cnt = Counter(garments_per_outfit)\n",
        "print(f\"\\n👕 Distribución: {dict(sorted(cnt.items()))}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Promedio: {np.mean(garments_per_outfit):.2f}, Mediana: {np.median(garments_per_outfit):.2f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Análisis de Resoluciones de Imágenes\n",
        "\n",
        "Una de las métricas más importantes para un pipeline VTON es la resolución de las imágenes de entrada. Las imágenes muy pequeñas o muy grandes pueden afectar la calidad de la inferencia."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Extraemos información de resoluciones desde los metadatos\n",
        "# La estructura típica en Garments2Look incluye 'image_resolution' o similar\n",
        "resolutions = []\n",
        "resolution_sources = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, outfit in enumerate(outfits[:200]):  # Muestra primeros 200 para no slowdown\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        # Intentamos acceder a la resolución del outfit principal\n",
        "        # La clave exacta depende del JSON; probamos varias opciones\n",
        "        img_info = outfit.get('image_resolution', outfit.get('resolution', outfit.get('img_size', None)))\n",
        "        if img_info:\n",
        "            resolutions.append(tuple(img_info) if isinstance(img_info, list) else (img_info, img_info))\n",
        "            resolution_sources.append(f'outfit_{i}')\n",
        "    except:\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"📊 Muestras con resolución: {len(resolutions)}/{200}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if resolutions:\n",
        "    widths = [r[0] for r in resolutions]\n",
        "    heights = [r[1] for r in resolutions]\n",
        "    aspect_ratios = [w/h if h != 0 else 0 for w, h in resolutions]\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"📏 Anchos: min={min(widths)}, max={max(widths)}, promedio={sum(widths)/len(widths):.0f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"📐 Alturas: min={min(heights)}, max={max(heights)}, promedio={sum(heights)/len(heights):.0f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"📐 Aspect ratios: min={min(aspect_ratios):.2f}, max={max(aspect_ratios):.2f}, promedio={sum(aspect_ratios)/len(aspect_ratios):.2f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Distribución de aspect ratios\n",
        "    import seaborn as sns\n",
        "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "    sns.histplot(aspect_ratios, bins=30, kde=True)\n",
        "    plt.title('Distribución de Aspect Ratios (primeros 200 outfits)')\n",
        "    plt.xlabel('Aspect ratio (width/height)')\n",
        "    plt.ylabel('Frecuencia')\n",
        "    plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n",
        "    plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Galería Visual de Outfits\n",
        "\n",
        "Mostramos una selección de outfits del dataset con su estructura de prendas. Como las imágenes reales no podemosDescargarlas todas (son las 284 GB), mostramos la información estructural y placeholders para las imágenes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Seleccionamos outfits para la galería (máximo 9 para un grid 3x3)\n",
        "gallery_count = min(9, len(outfits_mvp))\n",
        "gallery_outfits = outfits_mvp[:gallery_count]\n",
        "\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 3, figsize=(12, 10))\n",
        "fig.suptitle('Muestra de Outfits del Dataset (Info Estructural)', fontsize=16)\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, outfit in enumerate(gallery_outfits):\n",
        "    row, col = divmod(i, 3)\n",
        "    ax = axes[row, col]\n",
        "\n",
        "    n_prendas = len(outfit.get('garments', []))\n",
        "    outfit_id = outfit.get('outfit_id', i)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Mostramos info textual en lugar de imagen (para no descargar GB)\n",
        "    info_text = (f\"Outfit {outfit_id}\\n\"\n",
        "               f\"Prendas: {n_prendas}\\n\"\n",
        "               f\"Categorías: {', '.join([g.get('category', '?') for g in outfit.get('garments', [])])}\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax.text(0.5, 0.5, info_text, ha='center', va='center',\n",
        "            fontsize=10, wrap=True,\n",
        "            bbox=dict(boxstyle='round', facecolor='lightgray', alpha=0.7))\n",
        "    ax.set_title(f'Outfit {i+1}\\n{n_prendas} prendas', fontsize=8)\n",
        "    ax.axis('off')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fill remaining subplots if fewer than 9 outfits\n",
        "for i in range(gallery_count, 9):\n",
        "    row, col = divmod(i, 3)\n",
        "    axes[row, col].set_visible(False)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Distribución de Categorías Profundidad\n",
        "\n",
        "Análisis más detallado de las categorías de prendas, incluyendo subcategorías y su frecuencia."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Análisis completo de categorías\n",
        "all_cats = []\n",
        "all_subcats = []\n",
        "for o in outfits_mvp:  # Solo outfits MVP para el análisis\n",
        "    for g in o.get('garments', []):\n",
        "        all_cats.append(g.get('category', 'unknown'))\n",
        "        all_subcats.append(g.get('subcategory', 'unknown'))\n",
        "\n",
        "cat_cnt = Counter(all_cats)\n",
        "subcat_cnt = Counter(all_subcats)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"📂 Categorías principales (outfits MVP):\")\n",
        "for cat, count in cat_cnt.most_common():\n",
        "    print(f\"  {cat}: {count}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\n🔖 Top 15 subcategorías:\")\n",
        "for subcat, count in subcat_cnt.most_common(15):\n",
        "    print(f\"  {subcat}: {count}\")\n",
        "\n",
        # Gráfica de categorías\n        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "sns.barplot(x=list(cat_cnt.keys()), y=list(cat_cnt.values()))\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
        "plt.title('Distribución de Categorías (Outfits MVP)')\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Estadísticas de Outfit Completo\n",
        "\n",
        "Resumen integral de cada outfit: número de prendas, categorías mezcladas, y otras propiedades del metadato."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Calculamos estadísticas completas por outfit\n",
        "outfit_stats = []\n",
        "for o in outfits_mvp[:100]:  # Primeros 100 para resumen\n",
        "    garments = o.get('garments', [])\n",
        "    categories = [g.get('category', '?') for g in garments]\n",
        "    subcategories = [g.get('subcategory', '?') for g in garments]\n",
        "\n",
        "    stats = {\n",
        "        'outfit_id': o.get('outfit_id', 'N/A'),\n",
        "        'n_prendas': len(garments),\n",
        "        'categorias': categories,\n",
        "        'subcategorias': subcategories,\n",
        "        'has_accessory': any('accesorio' in str(s).lower() or 'shoe' in str(s).lower() for s in subcategories),\n",
        "        'has_outerwear': any(s in ['chaqueta', 'jacket', 'blazer'] for s in subcategories)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    outfit_stats.append(stats)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"📊 Resumen de {len(outfit_stats)} outfits MVP:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  - Prendas promedio: {np.mean([s['n_prendas'] for s in outfit_stats]):.2f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  - Con accesorios: {sum(1 for s in outfit_stats if s['has_accessory'])} ({100*sum(1 for s in outfit_stats if s['has_accessory'])/len(outfit_stats):.1f}%)\")\n",
        "print(f\"  - Con outerwear: {sum(1 for s in outfit_stats if s['has_outerwear'])} ({100*sum(1 for s in outfit_stats if s['has_outerwear'])/len(outfit_stats):.1f}%)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Conteo de combinaciones de categorías más comunes\n",
        "from itertools import combinations\n",
        "cat_combos = []\n",
        "for s in outfit_stats:\n",
        "    if len(s['categorias']) >= 2:\n",
        "        combo = tuple(sorted(s['categorias']))\n",
        "        cat_combos.append(combo)\n",
        "\n",
        "combo_cnt = Counter(cat_combos)\n",
        "print(f\"\\n🔀 Top 5 combinaciones de categorías:\")\n",
        "for combo, count in combo_cnt.most_common(5):\n",
        "    print(f\"  {combo}: {count}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Preparación para DWPose (Notebook 03)\n",
        "\n",
        "Este sección extrae información sobre las imágenes de persona que usaremos en el próximo notebook para la detección de keypoints con DWPose. Identificamos qué outfits tienen información de persona/image disponible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Identificamos qué outfits tienen referencia de persona/image\n",
        "persona_outfits = []\n",
        "for i, o in enumerate(outfits[:100]):\n",
        "    # Buscamos keys que indiquen imagen de persona\n",
        "    keys = list(o.keys())\n",
        "    has_person = any(k.lower().persona in k.lower() or k.lower().person in k.lower() for k in keys)\n",
        "    # O si tiene campo 'person_image' o similar\n        has_person2 = 'person_image' in o or 'persona_image' in o\n",
        "        \n",
        "    if has_person or has_person2:\n",
        "        persona_outfits.append({\n",
        "            'index': i,\n",
        "            'outfit_id': o.get('outfit_id', i),\n",
        "            'keys': [k for k in o.keys() if 'person' in k.lower() or 'image' in k.lower()][:5]  # primeras 5 keys relacionadas\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"👤 Outfits con información de persona en los primeros 100: {len(persona_outfits)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if persona_outfits:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nEjemplos de keys relacionadas con persona:\")\n",
        "    for po in persona_outfits[:3]:\n",
        "        print(f\"  Outfit {po['outfit_id']}: keys = {po['keys']}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**⚠️ Nota:** En modo execution real, al correr las siguientes celdas (Notebook 03) se importaría `dwpose` y se procesarían las imágenes de persona. En este notebook mantenemos el análisis estructural y preparación de datos."
      ]
    }
